CERAMIC SAFETY NOTICE

Glaze Lab calculates glaze recipes, unity molecular formulas, colour
predictions, property estimates and "food-safe" adjustments from
published material analyses and simplified chemistry heuristics. These
outputs are untested starting points for your own experiments. They are
not laboratory results and must not be relied on as such.

  * Fire every recipe on test tiles in your own kiln before using it on
    work. Results depend on your materials, clay body, kiln, firing
    schedule and atmosphere.

  * The food-safe mode only limits the amount of certain colourants. It
    cannot verify that a fired glaze is safe for surfaces that contact
    food or drink. Any such surface must be leach-tested (for example to
    ASTM C738 / ISO 6486 or an equivalent standard) before use.

  * Many raw glaze materials are hazardous to handle: silica dust,
    manganese, cobalt, chromium, copper, barium, lithium and others.
    Follow your supplier's safety data sheets and local regulations;
    use respiratory, eye and skin protection.

  * Material analyses are nominal supplier values and vary from batch
    to batch.

